    "body": "Adds ADR-009, which decides that we implement a CSS stylesheet parser ourselves in a new `renderer/css/stylesheet.{hpp,cpp}` rather than using lexbor's CSS module.\n\n## Why\n\nSame reasoning as ADR-007 and ADR-008: coupling our cascade to lexbor's CSS data structures (or reverse-converting on each parse) defeats the isolation we just built. The cascade needs our own typed `Declaration`/`Rule` model, which we will extend with computed values in Phase 3.\n\n## Scope of v1\n\n- Rule sets: `selector { declarations }`\n- Declarations: `property: value ;` with optional `!important`\n- Block comments (`/* ... */`) stripped\n- CSS 2.1 error recovery: skip malformed rules and declarations, never fail the whole stylesheet\n\n## Deferred\n\n- At-rules: `@media`, `@import`, `@font-face`, `@supports`\n- Custom properties (`--x`), `var()`, `calc()`, `rgb()`\n- Shorthand expansion (`margin: 0 1em` stays as a raw string; expansion happens at cascade time)\n\n## Public API\n\n`Stylesheet::parse(std::string_view) -> Stylesheet` — always returns a valid `Stylesheet`, never `nullopt`. Bad input yields fewer rules, matching browser behavior.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- New files: `src/renderer/css/stylesheet.hpp`, `stylesheet.cpp`, `tests/test_stylesheet.cpp`\n- No new lexbor includes. ADR-007 isolation invariant still holds.\n- `renderer::dom` and `SelectorList::parse` untouched — the CSS parser calls the selector parser, does not reimplement it.\n\n## Next\n\nOnce ADR-009 merges, the implementation issue will be \"Implement CSS stylesheet parser per ADR-009\" — two commits (rule parsing, then declaration parsing), same rhythm as #101.\n",
